1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,200
Peeling — or product pilling?

2
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:02,600
Those white flakes may not
be your skin.

3
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:05,500
Product residue rolls into
balls while you layer.

4
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:07,400
Not automatically the
product's fault.

5
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:09,200
Peeling is different —
actual skin flaking.

6
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:10,200
Dryness, tightness,
redness, stinging.

7
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:11,200
Bare skin vs.
after layering.

8
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:12,200
Flakes mean peeling.
Crumbs mean pilling.

9
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:13,200
A clue — not a diagnosis.

10
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:14,500
Try this: thin passes,
let it settle, pat don't rub.

11
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:15,800
Same total SPF —
just thinner passes.

12
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:17,100
One active at a time.
Moisturize. Protect.

13
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:19,100
Severe burning or swelling?
Stop and ask a doctor.

14
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:20,100
Bare skin → peeling.
After layering → pilling.

15
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:21,100
Save this test for
your next routine.
